{
  "$comment": "Golden sample events. These are not disconnected fixtures: stories A and B are two complete order journeys told end to end, so that reading this file top to bottom shows how correlation_id ties a transaction together and how causation_id records what caused what. Every event type in events/schemas/ appears at least once. These samples are validated by `npm test` in this directory and are reused as fixtures by the Pact contract tests in contracts/.",

  "stories": {
    "A": "Happy path. Ada orders two widgets and a gizmo; stock is reserved, payment is authorized and captured, the reservation is committed, the order is confirmed and Ada is emailed.",
    "B": "Compensation path. Grace orders one widget. Stock is reserved and payment is captured, but committing the reservation fails. The saga compensates in reverse: refund the payment, release the stock, cancel the order. The cancellation email then fails to send, which changes nothing upstream.",
    "C": "Reservation refused for want of stock.",
    "D": "Authorization declined by the PSP.",
    "E": "A reservation left behind by a dead saga, reclaimed by the expiry sweeper."
  },

  "$convention": "Stories C and D show a single event each, so the OrderPlaced that caused them is not reproduced here. Their causation_id ends in all zeros to stand for that omitted origin event. Story E has no causation_id at all, which is correct: the expiry sweeper acts on a timer, not in response to an event.",

